WEBVTT

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:24.066
Ah, another successful day.

00:00:24.149 --> 00:00:26.318
Deliveries were made,
nobody got hurt.

00:00:28.946 --> 00:00:31.406
Yes, another successful day.

00:00:32.324 --> 00:00:34.284
Well, see you guys tomorrow!

00:00:34.368 --> 00:00:36.954
I'm going home, by myself,

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.497
as is normal for me.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.998
Have a good night, Leela!

00:00:40.082 --> 00:00:41.834
I won't see you again
until the morning.

00:00:41.917 --> 00:00:43.585
- Good-bye. Good-bye now.
- Yeah, see you later, chumps.

00:00:43.669 --> 00:00:44.878
Okay, everybody,
see you tomorrow.

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.165
Good night, everyone!

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.375
Professor, you live here.

00:00:50.459 --> 00:00:51.752
Where are you going?

00:00:51.835 --> 00:00:53.628
I have no idea!

00:00:58.098 --> 00:00:58.833
Fry?

00:00:59.226 --> 00:01:01.061
Where are you?

00:01:01.163 --> 00:01:03.082
Right here, baby.

00:01:04.356 --> 00:01:05.983
Uh, could you help me?

00:01:07.401 --> 00:01:09.945
Ah, alone and unhooked.

00:01:10.028 --> 00:01:12.739
Let the evening begin.

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:18.328
All right, all right,
where's the surprise?

00:01:18.412 --> 00:01:20.664
Almost there.
Keep your eyeball closed.

00:01:25.961 --> 00:01:28.547
Fry, this is amazing!

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:30.481
You did this all by yourself?

00:01:30.506 --> 00:01:33.135
Uh-huh!
All with stuff I found around the office.

00:01:33.218 --> 00:01:35.429
Top Ramen in a Cremora sauce...

00:01:35.512 --> 00:01:37.389
Xerox-blackened chicken...

00:01:38.265 --> 00:01:39.391
Oh, and for dessert,

00:01:39.474 --> 00:01:41.602
cherry throat lozenge jubilee.

00:01:45.147 --> 00:01:46.899
What a wonderful nighttime
sneezing coughing

00:01:46.982 --> 00:01:49.026
stuffy head so-I-can-rest-dessert!

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:51.069
This really is lovely, Fry.

00:01:51.153 --> 00:01:52.404
Thank you.

00:01:58.702 --> 00:01:59.953
Uh-huh.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:03.248
Don't pay me no mind.

00:02:03.332 --> 00:02:06.877
Oh, Scruffy, could we please
have a little privacy here?

00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:11.673
If you can't see me,
is that private?

00:02:13.425 --> 00:02:15.260
Come on, let's go somewhere
we can be alone.

00:02:19.723 --> 00:02:21.391
It's so quiet.

00:02:21.475 --> 00:02:24.186
I'm surprised we're the only
couple out in Central Park.

00:02:24.269 --> 00:02:26.813
In this remote, unlit area.

00:02:26.897 --> 00:02:29.008
On Batman's night off. Oh!

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:30.234
This is a stickup!

00:02:30.317 --> 00:02:31.735
Oh, hey, Fry and Leela.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.487
Bender?
What are you doing?

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:36.406
I'm just out for my
nightly crime spree.

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:39.868
Which reminds me, this is
still a mugging, so...

00:02:39.952 --> 00:02:41.620
- Hee-ya!
- Ow!

00:02:41.703 --> 00:02:43.622
Ow!

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:46.111
Help, I'm being mugged!

00:02:55.551 --> 00:02:57.886
Mmm. A secluded table,

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:00.722
some big giant ants, and thou.

00:03:01.777 --> 00:03:03.070
Ow!

00:03:03.642 --> 00:03:05.269
Hello! I'm Dr. Zoidberg.

00:03:05.352 --> 00:03:07.646
I'll be your busboy tonight.

00:03:07.729 --> 00:03:08.939
Fry! Leela!

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.023
It's me, Zoidberg.

00:03:10.107 --> 00:03:11.650
From work, and LinkedIn?

00:03:11.733 --> 00:03:13.569
Mind if I join you?

00:03:13.652 --> 00:03:15.224
Very much so.

00:03:15.517 --> 00:03:18.915
What with the bad economy
and Hermes never paying me,

00:03:19.091 --> 00:03:21.201
I got a second job
clearing dishes.

00:03:21.285 --> 00:03:24.079
Dishes, dishes, dishes

00:03:24.162 --> 00:03:26.665
Cleaning up the dishes

00:03:26.748 --> 00:03:28.667
I'm a singing busboy.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:30.127
No, you're not!

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.962
Let's just go
to my place.

00:03:40.012 --> 00:03:42.556
Finally,
just the two of us.

00:03:42.639 --> 00:03:45.517
Yeah, I knew it was on
one of these albums.

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:47.936
Just the two of us

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.480
We can make it if we try

00:03:50.564 --> 00:03:52.024
Just the two of us...

00:03:52.107 --> 00:03:54.193
Uh, what about...

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:59.448
He won't wake up
if we stay quiet.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.536
Ooh.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:05.829
Ah!

00:04:05.913 --> 00:04:07.331
Nibbler! Scat!

00:04:10.292 --> 00:04:11.668
Why is it so impossible

00:04:11.752 --> 00:04:14.087
for two people to be completely alone?

00:04:14.171 --> 00:04:16.131
Are you and another person

00:04:16.215 --> 00:04:18.926
finding it impossible
to be completely alone?

00:04:19.009 --> 00:04:20.177
Now what?

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.762
It's targeted advertising.

00:04:21.845 --> 00:04:23.347
Can you shut it off?

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:24.973
Only if I cut off my arm.

00:04:25.057 --> 00:04:26.517
I'll get a knife.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.727
For true privacy and solitude,

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:32.231
visit Casa Ysolata Eco-Resort.

00:04:32.314 --> 00:04:35.234
From the moment our automated
shuttle picks you up,

00:04:35.317 --> 00:04:37.528
you'll be totally alone.

00:04:37.611 --> 00:04:41.240
With no employees and just a
single well-appointed bungalow,

00:04:41.323 --> 00:04:45.244
Casa Ysolata caters to only
one couple at a time.

00:04:45.327 --> 00:04:46.537
So act now!

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:48.622
The perfect getaway awaits!

00:04:48.705 --> 00:04:49.957
That sounds great!

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:53.585
Aw, but you can't possibly afford to
take me to a place like that.

00:04:53.669 --> 00:04:55.629
Oh, yes, she can.

00:04:55.712 --> 00:04:59.091
As a return guest, Leela will
receive a 25% discount

00:04:59.174 --> 00:05:01.510
and a complimentary waterfall.

00:05:01.694 --> 00:05:03.737
This is exactly what we need!

00:05:03.873 --> 00:05:06.465
Plus, you get a return visitor discount.

00:05:06.548 --> 00:05:08.800
Hey, wait, you were there before?

00:05:08.884 --> 00:05:10.385
Um, well...

00:05:10.469 --> 00:05:11.803
With someone else?

00:05:11.887 --> 00:05:14.347
Once.
With my old boyfriend Sean.

00:05:14.431 --> 00:05:16.016
But look, that's ancient history,

00:05:16.099 --> 00:05:18.018
and we need some
one-on-one time.

00:05:18.101 --> 00:05:19.603
I'm up for it if you are.

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:21.063
I don't know.

00:05:21.146 --> 00:05:23.423
You'd probably be thinking
of Sean the whole time.

00:05:23.448 --> 00:05:25.450
Oh, not the whole time.

00:05:31.398 --> 00:05:33.400
Who ordered all
these old-timey cars?

00:05:33.483 --> 00:05:35.861
The inhabitants of Simian 7,

00:05:35.944 --> 00:05:37.988
the Planet of the Apes.

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.614
And monkeys.

00:05:39.698 --> 00:05:41.575
And tarsiers, and several lemurs.

00:05:41.658 --> 00:05:44.202
All primates, really.

00:05:44.286 --> 00:05:46.455
Hey, guys.
We just stopped by to tell you

00:05:46.538 --> 00:05:48.081
we're taking some
vacation days.

00:05:48.165 --> 00:05:49.333
No, you're not!

00:05:49.416 --> 00:05:50.751
You've got to
go on this delivery!

00:05:50.834 --> 00:05:52.336
But we've earned these days off.

00:05:52.419 --> 00:05:54.546
We're not cattle, we're human beings.

00:05:54.629 --> 00:05:56.465
You're human beings?

00:05:56.548 --> 00:05:59.009
Good Lord, you can't go on this delivery.

00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:01.762
Humans are forbidden on
the Planet of the Primates!

00:06:01.845 --> 00:06:04.014
Okay, then.
See you in a week!

00:06:04.097 --> 00:06:05.640
Buh-bye!

00:06:05.724 --> 00:06:09.311
Bender, since you're not human,
you can still go.

00:06:09.394 --> 00:06:11.730
And, Zoidberg,
you can replace Fry.

00:06:11.813 --> 00:06:13.148
Hooray!

00:06:13.231 --> 00:06:15.233
I'm the Fry,
with the cool red jacket

00:06:15.317 --> 00:06:17.569
and the walking on sunshine!

00:06:17.653 --> 00:06:20.530
But we still need someone
to pilot the ship.

00:06:20.614 --> 00:06:21.907
Amy, what are you?

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:23.492
- Human.
- Damn!

00:06:23.575 --> 00:06:25.077
Then you'll need a disguise.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:27.037
Do you have a marmoset costume?

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.330
No.

00:06:28.413 --> 00:06:29.831
Just these marmoset pajamas.

00:06:29.915 --> 00:06:31.416
They'll have to do.

00:06:56.441 --> 00:06:59.152
Man, these hands do everything
but pick your nose.

00:07:02.698 --> 00:07:04.324
Wow. Well picked.

00:07:04.408 --> 00:07:06.451
I had a nice picking
last time I was here.

00:07:06.535 --> 00:07:08.161
Come on, let's take a walk.

00:07:08.245 --> 00:07:09.913
I'll show you around.

00:07:33.979 --> 00:07:37.357
Hey, want to go skinny-dipping
by the light of the fireflies?

00:07:37.441 --> 00:07:38.567
Leela!

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:41.320
Somebody might see Wingus
and the Ping Pong boys!

00:07:41.403 --> 00:07:43.280
No, it's just
the two of us.

00:07:43.363 --> 00:07:44.406
Come on!

00:07:49.511 --> 00:07:51.831
All right,
I'll just keep my top on.

00:07:53.062 --> 00:07:54.958
Oh, what the heck.

00:07:55.417 --> 00:07:56.585
Wooo!

00:07:59.713 --> 00:08:02.591
Well, here we are,
alone and naked.

00:08:02.674 --> 00:08:04.301
Want to play Marco Polo?

00:08:04.384 --> 00:08:05.469
Sure!

00:08:06.428 --> 00:08:08.180
- Marco!
- Polo!

00:08:08.263 --> 00:08:09.306
Marco!

00:08:09.389 --> 00:08:10.849
Polo!

00:08:12.809 --> 00:08:14.770
- Sean?
- Leela?

00:08:14.853 --> 00:08:17.314
- Sean?
- Polo!

00:08:28.116 --> 00:08:29.868
What are you doing here, Sean?

00:08:29.951 --> 00:08:31.036
I was on vacation.

00:08:31.119 --> 00:08:32.537
Repeat customer discount,

00:08:32.621 --> 00:08:34.581
free meals 'cause I brought
my own peanut butter.

00:08:34.665 --> 00:08:37.084
Whole trip cost less than 600 bucks.

00:08:37.167 --> 00:08:40.295
But this is a private resort
for only two people at a time.

00:08:40.379 --> 00:08:42.506
Yeah, my week is up,
but the shuttle broke down

00:08:42.589 --> 00:08:43.924
and they're still
trying to fix it.

00:08:46.259 --> 00:08:48.970
But, hey, they gave me two free
drink coupons for my trouble.

00:08:49.054 --> 00:08:50.639
You want to buy one?

00:08:50.969 --> 00:08:52.346
How about you?

00:08:52.371 --> 00:08:53.725
Sean, I'd like you to meet Fry.

00:08:53.972 --> 00:08:55.185
He and I are...

00:08:55.268 --> 00:08:56.812
What would you say we are, Fry?

00:08:56.895 --> 00:08:58.772
Nude and interrupted.

00:08:58.855 --> 00:09:01.400
Uh-huh.
Listen, Leela, I'd love to catch up.

00:09:01.483 --> 00:09:03.610
What do ya say we split
a free drink at the robo-bar?

00:09:03.694 --> 00:09:05.195
They've got unlimited pretzels.

00:09:05.278 --> 00:09:08.198
Put a little peanut butter on there,
they really fill you up.

00:09:08.281 --> 00:09:10.325
Well, it has been a while.

00:09:10.409 --> 00:09:11.785
Is it okay with you, Fry?

00:09:11.868 --> 00:09:13.412
Sure, that'd be great.

00:09:13.495 --> 00:09:15.539
I'll just sit here
and feed the mosquitoes.

00:09:42.274 --> 00:09:45.152
I'm not sure this marmoset
disguise is working.

00:09:45.235 --> 00:09:46.778
I'm not sure either.

00:09:46.862 --> 00:09:48.238
We'd better ask Amy.

00:09:49.531 --> 00:09:51.158
Well, that's the last one.

00:09:51.241 --> 00:09:53.660
But what does a monkey
financial-services corporation

00:09:53.744 --> 00:09:55.704
want with a fleet
of classic cars?

00:09:55.787 --> 00:09:58.582
We don't want the cars,
just the tires!

00:09:58.665 --> 00:10:01.293
Gentlemen, the new
office chairs are here.

00:10:12.846 --> 00:10:14.264
Sign here, please.

00:10:14.348 --> 00:10:17.392
I'll just use
my opposable thumb.

00:10:18.352 --> 00:10:20.937
You know, normally I don't
go for New World monkeys,

00:10:21.021 --> 00:10:23.899
but I am digging
your upright posture.

00:10:23.982 --> 00:10:27.069
Geez, Edwards, hitting on
a delivery marmoset?

00:10:27.152 --> 00:10:30.030
Why don't you just show
her your big blue ass?

00:10:30.113 --> 00:10:32.115
Oh, I'm getting to that.

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:36.286
Call me.

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:38.538
Oh, my gosh. Amy?

00:10:38.622 --> 00:10:40.332
- Amy Wong?
- Guenter?

00:10:40.415 --> 00:10:42.167
From Mars University?

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:43.794
How have you been?

00:10:43.877 --> 00:10:45.170
Ah, pretty good.

00:10:45.253 --> 00:10:46.755
Working in financial services,

00:10:46.838 --> 00:10:48.465
you really get
to help rich people

00:10:48.548 --> 00:10:50.467
realize their expensive dreams.

00:10:51.718 --> 00:10:53.470
Nice disguise, by the way.

00:10:53.553 --> 00:10:55.138
I won't say anything.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:03.480
After that, my music career
really started taking off.

00:11:03.563 --> 00:11:05.649
I recorded a demo
and shot a video,

00:11:05.732 --> 00:11:07.150
but then I lost my phone.

00:11:07.234 --> 00:11:09.277
My life has been
equally exciting.

00:11:09.361 --> 00:11:12.823
It turned out, I'm not
an alien orphan, I'm a mutant.

00:11:12.906 --> 00:11:14.574
With wonderful parents.

00:11:14.658 --> 00:11:17.666
Yeah, we've been through
a lot, me and my sax.

00:11:17.696 --> 00:11:19.114
May I noodle?

00:11:19.413 --> 00:11:21.748
Please.
It's been a long time.

00:11:37.923 --> 00:11:39.049
Look at them.

00:11:39.132 --> 00:11:41.718
I came here to get romantic
with the woman I love.

00:11:41.802 --> 00:11:44.262
Instead, she's with her
ex-boyfriend and I'm stuck with

00:11:44.346 --> 00:11:46.181
a pair of skilled
mechanical hands.

00:11:48.016 --> 00:11:50.727
Say, I don't suppose
you're free later?

00:11:52.229 --> 00:11:54.022
Then I have no choice.

00:11:54.815 --> 00:11:56.817
And now this part.

00:12:01.822 --> 00:12:05.117
If you want to steal my girl,
you'll have to fight me for her.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:07.828
Stop playing that lovely song
and put up your dukes!

00:12:09.496 --> 00:12:11.331
Fry, there's nothing
to be jealous of.

00:12:11.415 --> 00:12:13.792
I've been sitting here
paying my bills online.

00:12:16.586 --> 00:12:18.714
Dude, you
broke my reed!

00:12:18.797 --> 00:12:20.090
You owe me, like, a dollar!

00:12:20.173 --> 00:12:22.259
You'll have to kill me for it!

00:12:22.342 --> 00:12:23.719
Hi-yah!

00:12:25.637 --> 00:12:27.180
Just stop, you two!

00:12:27.264 --> 00:12:28.932
I've had that reed for 20 years!

00:12:29.016 --> 00:12:30.851
It's irreplaceable!

00:12:32.227 --> 00:12:33.353
I want my dollar!

00:12:33.437 --> 00:12:34.688
Sean?

00:12:34.771 --> 00:12:36.523
What the heck are you doing, you moron?

00:12:36.607 --> 00:12:38.108
A little drinking,
a little fighting.

00:12:38.191 --> 00:12:40.485
- Get off my back.
- Who are you?

00:12:40.569 --> 00:12:41.945
This is my wife, Darlene.

00:12:42.029 --> 00:12:43.488
We met at the 99-cent store.

00:12:43.572 --> 00:12:44.781
You're married?

00:12:44.865 --> 00:12:46.658
Wait a dang minute.

00:12:46.742 --> 00:12:49.620
One eye, purple hair... You're Leela!

00:12:49.703 --> 00:12:51.371
The crazy one that Sean dumped.

00:12:51.455 --> 00:12:52.914
It was mutual!

00:12:52.998 --> 00:12:55.584
Sean, why is this hussy at our resort?

00:12:55.667 --> 00:12:58.420
Your resort? This is our vacation.

00:12:58.503 --> 00:13:00.464
- Could've fooled me.
- Quiet, Fry.

00:13:00.547 --> 00:13:02.841
This is between me and the
lady in the hooter hammock.

00:13:02.924 --> 00:13:03.967
Listen, honey,

00:13:04.051 --> 00:13:06.011
I'd love to stay here
and Denny's-fight you,

00:13:06.094 --> 00:13:07.679
but they just told me
the shuttle's fixed.

00:13:07.763 --> 00:13:09.014
What? We better leave

00:13:09.097 --> 00:13:10.432
before they charge
us for another day.

00:13:10.515 --> 00:13:12.809
Grab some complimentary snacks
and let's go!

00:13:17.481 --> 00:13:20.901
I'm drunk, I'm grouchy, and I'm
gonna eat this peanut butter.

00:13:20.984 --> 00:13:22.569
Want to watch?

00:13:22.653 --> 00:13:24.446
Not really, but I will.

00:13:24.529 --> 00:13:25.739
Fine.

00:13:41.296 --> 00:13:44.299
This is Christopher Colobus,
the brave monkey

00:13:44.383 --> 00:13:47.219
who led a band of genetically-engineered
primates from Earth

00:13:47.302 --> 00:13:49.054
to colonize our planet.

00:13:49.137 --> 00:13:50.889
Wait, if you guys came from Earth,

00:13:50.973 --> 00:13:52.474
why do you hate humans so much?

00:13:52.557 --> 00:13:53.934
Oh, please.

00:13:54.017 --> 00:13:57.104
Humans experimented on us,
chained us to organ-grinders,

00:13:57.187 --> 00:14:00.190
made us ride around
in ridiculous tiny vehicles.

00:14:02.567 --> 00:14:05.654
You're still riding around
in ridiculous tiny vehicles.

00:14:05.737 --> 00:14:06.863
By choice.

00:14:06.947 --> 00:14:08.699
Come on, let's grab some lunch.

00:14:12.286 --> 00:14:15.163
It's all-you-can-eat, so just
pick off whatever looks good.

00:14:16.581 --> 00:14:18.333
Ew, gross!

00:14:18.417 --> 00:14:20.252
I'm gonna use the tongs.

00:14:24.589 --> 00:14:27.384
We have our own literature, music and art.

00:14:27.467 --> 00:14:30.178
The smear lines are impeccable.

00:14:32.472 --> 00:14:34.558
Unlike your Earth zoos,

00:14:34.641 --> 00:14:37.269
our zoo is a model of
compassionate encagement.

00:14:37.352 --> 00:14:39.646
The animals don't even
know they're in captivity.

00:14:43.775 --> 00:14:44.860
See?

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:51.199
Um...

00:14:51.283 --> 00:14:52.492
Leela?

00:14:52.576 --> 00:14:54.036
I'm sorry I ruined
our vacation.

00:14:55.203 --> 00:14:56.663
It's not your fault.

00:14:56.747 --> 00:14:58.415
I wanted this week to be special.

00:14:58.498 --> 00:15:00.709
And then Sean had to show up.

00:15:00.792 --> 00:15:03.378
Do you still have feelings for him?

00:15:03.462 --> 00:15:04.259
No.

00:15:04.435 --> 00:15:08.050
I mean, I'll always respect
his frugality, but that's all.

00:15:08.133 --> 00:15:11.887
Well, the important thing is,
we're finally alone.

00:15:30.113 --> 00:15:32.324
Oh, your God!

00:15:32.407 --> 00:15:34.943
Fry and Leela
are in a zoo!

00:15:35.067 --> 00:15:36.110
Shh!

00:15:36.253 --> 00:15:37.462
Oh, sorry.

00:15:42.167 --> 00:15:43.251
Wow.

00:15:43.335 --> 00:15:45.003
Those fireflies are going nuts.

00:15:45.087 --> 00:15:46.171
Come here.

00:15:46.254 --> 00:15:48.256
I've always wanted
to make love by bug-light.

00:15:49.424 --> 00:15:51.176
Shmoly crap!

00:15:51.259 --> 00:15:53.762
We've got to get Fry and Leela
out of this habitat

00:15:53.845 --> 00:15:55.472
before they humiliate themselves.

00:15:55.555 --> 00:15:59.184
Please, Amy, the act of love
is a beautiful and natural...

00:15:59.268 --> 00:16:01.436
Oh, my God, cover your eyes!

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:03.897
Come on, we'd better talk
to the zoo director.

00:16:10.153 --> 00:16:12.322
Mr. Zoo Director,
we don't know you

00:16:12.406 --> 00:16:14.074
and you're facing away from us,

00:16:14.157 --> 00:16:16.034
but you have our friends
caged up and...

00:16:16.118 --> 00:16:18.161
Dr. Banjo?

00:16:18.245 --> 00:16:20.021
The same.

00:16:20.731 --> 00:16:21.505
Hang on.

00:16:21.999 --> 00:16:23.625
Coming around.

00:16:23.709 --> 00:16:25.043
There.

00:16:25.127 --> 00:16:27.879
Why, if it isn't
Professor Farnsworth's friends.

00:16:27.963 --> 00:16:30.007
Zoidberg, Bender and...

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:32.718
Who is this fetching
young marmoset?

00:16:32.801 --> 00:16:35.137
Uh, Sparkles?

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:36.888
Enough zoo director talk.

00:16:36.972 --> 00:16:39.224
We know those guys,
and we want them freed.

00:16:39.308 --> 00:16:41.977
Ah, yes, our famous
Human Habitat.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:44.646
This pair have been
our most popular specimens yet.

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:46.148
Especially the male.

00:16:46.231 --> 00:16:48.942
I've never seen one have
so much trouble with zippers.

00:16:49.026 --> 00:16:52.112
As fun as it is to watch Fry
try and operate his pants,

00:16:52.195 --> 00:16:54.656
you can't keep him and Leela
here against their will.

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:56.199
Against their will?

00:16:56.283 --> 00:16:58.744
My good robot,
they paid to be here.

00:16:58.827 --> 00:17:00.829
They think they're on
a romantic holiday.

00:17:00.912 --> 00:17:04.625
Humans have been vacationing
in our habitat for years.

00:17:04.708 --> 00:17:06.710
In fact,
Leela's been here before.

00:17:07.294 --> 00:17:09.171
When her previous mate, Sean,

00:17:09.254 --> 00:17:11.364
returned here
with his current female,

00:17:11.389 --> 00:17:14.809
we quickly invited Leela back
as a behavioral experiment,

00:17:14.893 --> 00:17:16.478
keeping the first pair here

00:17:16.561 --> 00:17:19.314
under the pretext
of shuttle repairs.

00:17:19.673 --> 00:17:21.925
The human exhibit
has never been so popular,

00:17:22.008 --> 00:17:24.052
all thanks to your friends.

00:17:24.136 --> 00:17:25.470
Well, that's that.

00:17:25.554 --> 00:17:26.805
What do you want to see next?

00:17:26.888 --> 00:17:28.390
We have a great maritime museum.

00:17:28.473 --> 00:17:29.766
Shut up, Guenter!

00:17:29.850 --> 00:17:32.185
You can't just put people on display.

00:17:32.269 --> 00:17:33.270
It's cruel.

00:17:33.353 --> 00:17:34.354
Cruel?

00:17:34.437 --> 00:17:37.514
Was it cruel when humans caged
other primates in zoos for centuries?

00:17:37.553 --> 00:17:39.776
Wait, I know the answer to this one.

00:17:40.289 --> 00:17:40.781
Yes.

00:17:40.965 --> 00:17:43.592
Look, we're all agreed humans are idiots.

00:17:43.735 --> 00:17:45.361
But these idiots are our friends.

00:17:45.399 --> 00:17:46.775
Friends, eh?

00:17:46.859 --> 00:17:48.652
Perhaps you wouldn't be
so worried about them

00:17:48.735 --> 00:17:51.154
if you knew what they really
thought of you.

00:17:51.238 --> 00:17:53.532
It's so great
being away from everyone.

00:17:53.615 --> 00:17:55.909
Zoidberg and his awful stench.

00:17:55.993 --> 00:17:57.244
Stanky.

00:17:57.327 --> 00:17:59.288
Bender and his obnoxious ego.

00:17:59.371 --> 00:18:00.706
But... But...

00:18:00.789 --> 00:18:02.291
And what about Amy?

00:18:02.374 --> 00:18:03.834
Always prancing around

00:18:03.917 --> 00:18:06.670
- in thosestupid marmoset pajamas.
- Hey!

00:18:06.753 --> 00:18:08.255
You know who I hate most?

00:18:08.338 --> 00:18:10.132
That monkey we haven't seen in years.

00:18:10.215 --> 00:18:11.508
Guenter.

00:18:12.593 --> 00:18:14.136
You see?

00:18:14.219 --> 00:18:16.930
Observing animals yields
critical scientific data.

00:18:17.014 --> 00:18:18.265
For example,

00:18:18.348 --> 00:18:20.517
that you, Sparkles the marmoset,

00:18:20.601 --> 00:18:22.644
are in fact Sparkles the human!

00:18:24.521 --> 00:18:26.899
Wild human!
Wild human!

00:18:29.026 --> 00:18:30.736
Dr. Banjo, surely we can

00:18:30.819 --> 00:18:33.280
discuss this like
recently civilized beings.

00:18:37.618 --> 00:18:39.286
Cheese it!

00:18:39.369 --> 00:18:41.288
Whoop-whoop-whoop-whoop.

00:18:46.793 --> 00:18:47.794
Hurry!

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:49.630
We still have to rescue Fry and Leela!

00:18:49.713 --> 00:18:51.965
Even if my stupid marmoset pajamas

00:18:52.049 --> 00:18:53.842
offend Leela's big fat eye.

00:18:53.926 --> 00:18:57.012
After they said
I had an obnoxious ego?

00:18:57.095 --> 00:18:58.972
Me, the magnificent Bender?

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:01.350
Back!

00:19:01.433 --> 00:19:02.768
Back, you beasts!

00:19:02.851 --> 00:19:03.894
Follow me.

00:19:03.977 --> 00:19:05.270
The one who stinks,

00:19:05.354 --> 00:19:06.855
according to Fry's
delicate nose.

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:13.320
This way. We can get in

00:19:13.403 --> 00:19:14.696
through the back
of the human cage and...

00:19:16.992 --> 00:19:18.785
Prairie elephant!

00:19:18.909 --> 00:19:20.953
Adorable prairie elephant!

00:19:26.291 --> 00:19:28.043
Whoop-whoop-whoop-whoop.

00:19:39.263 --> 00:19:41.098
Okay, let's just get in,
get out and...

00:19:44.935 --> 00:19:46.687
Now what?

00:19:46.770 --> 00:19:49.565
Now we wait for nature
to take its course.

00:19:49.648 --> 00:19:52.109
How long does it take
to pass through a moon worm?

00:19:56.196 --> 00:19:58.866
All right, let's just rescue
them and get out of here.

00:20:07.291 --> 00:20:09.877
Hooray, they're saved!

00:20:16.975 --> 00:20:19.853
And the robot hands would make
you a strawberry shortcake

00:20:19.937 --> 00:20:21.355
any time of day.

00:20:21.438 --> 00:20:23.857
4:00, 7:00, any time.

00:20:23.941 --> 00:20:25.067
No way!

00:20:25.150 --> 00:20:26.151
I'm not lying.

00:20:26.235 --> 00:20:27.527
Also, Leela and I...

00:20:27.611 --> 00:20:31.156
Had a very nice,
very private vacation.

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:33.200
Let's just leave
it at that.

00:20:33.283 --> 00:20:34.493
Oh, can I tell them?

00:20:34.576 --> 00:20:35.577
Please, please?

00:20:35.661 --> 00:20:36.745
I got to tell them.

00:20:36.828 --> 00:20:38.914
No. You'll only make them feel bad.

00:20:38.997 --> 00:20:40.666
Let's not humiliate them.

00:20:40.749 --> 00:20:42.542
Listen to Sparkles.

00:20:42.626 --> 00:20:43.961
Oh, no.

00:20:44.044 --> 00:20:46.463
What happened to
your marmoset pajamas, Amy?

00:20:46.546 --> 00:20:50.425
Fry and I were just talking
about how adorable those are.

00:20:51.969 --> 00:20:54.263
Also, nothing in here
smells like a rotting crab.

00:20:56.414 --> 00:20:58.058
Now can I? Now can I?

00:20:58.141 --> 00:20:59.476
Let 'er rip.

00:21:03.480 --> 00:21:04.982
You were in a zoo!